\begin{proof}
For each $i \in \{1, \ldots, T\}$, let $c_i$ be a $k$-coloring of $G_{i-1}\cup G_i\cup G_{i+1}$ such that if $i$ is odd,  $c_i:V\rightarrow \{1, \ldots, k\}$ and if $i$ is even, $c_i:V\rightarrow\{k+1, \ldots, 2k\}$. By construction, each $c_i$ is a proper coloring of $(G_{i-1}\cup G_i\cup G_{i+1})\leq k$. For all $i \in [T]$, for all $u,v \in V, c_i(u) \neq c_{i+1} (v)$. Hence $c_i$ and $c_{i+1}$ are compatible in the graph $G_i \cup G_{i+1}$ for all $i \in [T]$. Therefore the sequence $(c_1,\ldots,c_T)$ is a temporal $2k$-coloring of $\mathcal{G}$.
