In this section, we restrict all snapshots to some classical  classes of graphs. We choose classes where the coloring questions are well known. The classes we consider are trees, paths, graphs with bounded degeneracy and graphs with bounded degree. For all those cases, we provide better bounds for the temporal chromatic number, in particular through the analysis of the smashing of 3 snapshots.

We start with a quick analysis for the case where each snapshot is a bipartite graph.


