\vspace{2ex}

The following result is about online temporal coloring, and give some information for the open question whether 7 colors are needed to color a temporal tree. We show that there exists some 6-coloring $c_i$ for some well chosen snapshots up to $G_{i+1}$ and some $G_{i+2}$ such that any coloring $c_{i+1}$ needs at least 7 colors. It implies that, to compute an online temporal 6-coloring (if it is possible), choosing some $c_i$ that is just a coloring compatible with $c_{i-1}$ is not enough.


