    \item Since $c_i^2$ is compatible with $c_{i+1}^2$ in $G_{i+1}$ (Let $uv \in E_{i+1}$, then $x_{i+1}(u) \neq x_{i+1}(v)$. It implies that $c_i^2(v) \neq c_{i+1}^2(u)$.), $c_{i+1}^1$ and $c_{i+1}^2$ are compatible in $G_{i+1}$. Since $c_i^2 = c_{i+1}^1$, for all $i$, $c_i^2$ and $c_{i+1}^1$ are compatible in $G_i \cup G_{i+1}$.
\end{enumerate}
\end{proof}




