\subsection{Feedback with Confidence}
% Furthermore, to avoid over-correction, we obtain the confidence scores for fluent and GEC transcriptions of the models, and accept/reject edits based on these confidence scores.
To improve the reliability of SGEC feedback evaluation, we adopt an edit-level confidence filtering strategy (Section~\ref{sec:confidence_desc}). %This allows us to exclude low-confidence edits, those likely caused by ASR or GEC model uncertainty, from the evaluation process. Table~\ref{tab:edit_confidence_compare} shows the best F$_\text{0.5}$ scores across different confidence scoring methods, evaluated on the Whisper$_\text{gec+pt}$ (Orig) model.
This approach assigns a confidence score to each edit and discards those below a certain threshold, thereby reducing the influence of low-confidence edits, often caused by ASR or model uncertainty, on evaluation metrics.

