By our choice of $\mu(n)$, the right-hand side approaches $(1-\err)$ for large $n$, meaning that $M$ accepts $uw'v$ with probability greater than $\frac{1}{2}$. This contradicts the assumption that $M$ separates $A$ and $B$.
\end{proof}

