%Recently, transformer-based models have been adopted for pedestrian intention prediction by integrating multiple input modalities \cite{zhao2021action}\cite{achaji2022attention}\cite{zhou2023pit}\cite{lorenzo2021capformer}\cite{zhang2023trep}. Although these models have shown promise across various vision tasks, it is important to note that RNN-based feature fusion methods with multiple modalities often offer comparable performance. Moreover, RNN-based approaches tend to be more interpretable, which is crucial for understanding model decisions in safety-critical applications like pedestrian intention prediction.



