Although the SDBM satisfiability problem turns out to be \NP-hard, we are able to provide and algorithm that runs in $\Ocal(n m \Dlcm)$ time, where $n$ is the number of variables, $m$ is the number of constraints and $\Dlcm$ is the least common multiple of all congruence divisors. This time complexity, which is pseudo-linear in $\Dlcm$, is practical for program analysis applications. We also present an $\Ocal(n^4)$ complexity algorithm for HSDBM satisfiability.

