We now define the new abstract domains.

\begin{definition}
\label{def:SDBM}
A \emph{Strided DBM (SDBM)} is a DBM with additional constraints
\begin{align*}
x_i \equiv r_i \mod d_i && i \in [n]
\end{align*}
where all $d_i, r_i$ are in $\Zbb$. When referring to such a system, $\Dlcm$ will denote $\lcm(d_1, \dots d_n)$. Given an SDBM, we define the \emph{underlying DBM} as the constraint system without these congruence constraints.
\end{definition}
\noindent
Note that one may encode the lack of a congruence constraint as $x_i \equiv 0 \mod 1$.

\begin{definition}
\label{def:hSDBM}
A \emph{Harmonic SDBM (HSDBM)} constraint system is an SDBM where the congruence divisors are sorted and each one divides the next, i.e., $d_1 \mid d_2 \mid \dots \mid d_n$.
\end{definition}


\section{Satisfiability}

